IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g4-nouns.l4: the group-local nouns of Articles 11 and 12 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (group G4). DECLAREs only: no rule and no #EVAL live here.
-- The shared nouns (Entity, Registered charity, Standing on the register, Legal actor, Decision of the Commissioner) are in domain.l4 and are not redeclared.
-- Whether a thing is a fact a witness could testify to, or a rule, is the membership test of the skill: what is here is a fact about an application, a payment, a name or an act.
-- Every discretion of the Law ("in the opinion of the Commissioner", "satisfied", "prescribed") appears below as a Boolean field or input NAMED FOR WHAT IT DECIDES;
-- none of them is computed, and each module that reads one says so.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register: the nouns of Articles 11 and 12`

§§ `Article 11 -- the acts`

-- Who does what under Article 11, as a role and an act. The performer rule of the language applies: the first actor-typed field of an act is the party that may be obliged to it or permitted it.
-- The constructors are named for what is done, never for the Article that says so.
@ref Article 11 (the acts of the Article, by role)
DECLARE `Thing done under Article 11` IS ONE OF
    `apply to be registered`
    `provide the Commissioner with what Article 11(2) requires`
    `provide with the application the additional information that must be provided to the JFSC`
    `request to be registered under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
    `make Regulations prescribing other information, documents or evidence to be provided on an application`
    `make Regulations making further provision as to the procedure for making an application`
    `make Regulations prescribing further grounds on which an application must or may be refused`
    `make an Order providing for the period within which the Commissioner must decide an application`
    `make an Order providing for the notification of decisions and of reasons for refusal`
    `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) does not apply to a described applicant`
    `make an Order that a provision of Article 11(2) applies to a described applicant subject to a modification`
    `register the applicant as a charity`
    `refuse to register the applicant`
    `publish and maintain guidance on whether an activity is substantial`
    `consult, and publish a report on the consultation, before issuing or amending the guidance`
    `provide the Minister with a copy of the guidance and the report`
    `lay a copy of the guidance and the report before the States`
    `have regard to the guidance in determining whether an activity is substantial`
    `have regard to the guidance when performing a function to which it is relevant`
    `issue a certificate of registration` HAS `registered name` IS A STRING, `registration number` IS A STRING, `date of registration` IS A DATE
    `issue a further certificate for a new or alternative registered name` HAS name IS A STRING, `date entered on the register` IS A DATE
    `pass the request, with the information and documents, to the JFSC`
    `treat the request, with the information and documents, as an application for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`

@ref Article 11 (an act and the role that does it)
DECLARE `Act under Article 11` HAS
    actor IS A `Legal actor`
    `what is done` IS A `Thing done under Article 11`

§§ `Article 11(2) -- what the application must include`

-- (a) "information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to" three matters.
-- One of these records per matter: what was provided as at the application, whether the position once registered would differ, and what was provided as proposed once registered.
-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
@ref Article 11(2)(a) (src:301)
DECLARE `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` HAS
    `provided as at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would differ once the entity is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (e)(ii) "any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application": a payment, with the two facts about its payee that fork F4.11 reads.
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (src:310)
DECLARE `Payment to a governor` HAS
    `name of the payee` IS A STRING
    `date of the payment` IS A DATE
    `amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `payee was a governor when the payment was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payee is a governor on the date of the application` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order under Article 11(8)(b) may disapply or modify ("any provision of paragraph (2)"): one constructor per paragraph or sub-paragraph that states a requirement.
-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
-- src:302 | (i) how the entity meets the requirements of paragraphs (4)(c) and (d),
-- src:303 | (ii) the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (d) of Article 8(3), and
-- src:304 | (iii) if applicable, the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (h), (i), (m) and (n) of Article 8(3);
-- src:305 | (b) a copy of the applicant’s constitution;
-- src:306 | (c) a draft of the proposed statement of the entity’s registered charitable purposes;
-- src:307 | (d) a draft of the entity’s registered public benefit statement;
-- src:308 | (e) details of –
-- src:309 | (i) the applicant’s most recent, if any, financial accounts,
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
-- src:311 | (iii) any other financial information that would be required if the application were for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008, and
-- src:312 | (iv) if the applicant is not requesting entry in the restricted section of the register, any further financial information prescribed by the Minister by Order; and
-- src:313 | (f) such other information, documents and evidence as may be –
-- src:314 | (i) required by Regulations under paragraph (3), or
-- src:315 | (ii) otherwise requested by the Commissioner in order to determine the application.
@ref Article 11(2) (src:301-315)
DECLARE `Item of Article 11(2)` IS ONE OF
    `information and evidence on how the entity meets the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) and (d)`
    `information and evidence on the matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)`
    `information and evidence on the matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)`
    `a copy of the applicant's constitution`
    `a draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes`
    `a draft of the registered public benefit statement`
    `details of the applicant's most recent financial accounts`
    `details of payments to governors in the twelve months preceding the application`
    `a draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)`
    `other financial information required under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008`
    `further financial information prescribed by Order`
    `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations under Article 11(3)`
    `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner`

-- (a)(iii) is required only "if applicable"; the flag `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant` is TRUE when at least one of those matters applies, and the information is then what is
-- required about the matters that do apply.
-- The application as a record of facts, one sub-record per paragraph of Article 11(2): when it was lodged and when it became complete; for each requirement whether the item was provided
-- and, where the requirement is conditional, whether the condition holds. The Law's own conditions are separate fields: "if applicable" (a)(iii), "if any" (e)(i),
-- "if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies" (e)(ii) [that one is the standard input IP29, not a field], "if the applicant is not requesting entry in the restricted section" (e)(iv).
-- The content of the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008, of any Order and of any Regulations is not in the sources: whether they require something is an input.
-- "Complete" is the word of Article 19(6): an application is not complete if the entity has not complied with Article 19(5). That is a narrower thing than including everything Article 11(2) requires:
-- an application can be complete in this sense and still lack the copy of the constitution. Fork F4.2 (reading B) uses the day it became complete in THIS sense.
@ref Articles 11(2)(e)(ii), 11(8)(a)(i) and 19(6) (the day an application is lodged and the day it becomes complete)
DECLARE `Dates of an application` HAS
    `date lodged` IS A DATE
    `date on which it became complete` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:301 | (a) information and evidence, as at the time of the application and (if different) as proposed once the entity is registered, as to –
-- src:302 | (i) how the entity meets the requirements of paragraphs (4)(c) and (d),
-- src:303 | (ii) the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (d) of Article 8(3), and
-- src:304 | (iii) if applicable, the matters that are required to be registered under sub-paragraphs (h), (i), (m) and (n) of Article 8(3);
@ref Article 11(2)(a) (src:301-304)
DECLARE `Particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` HAS
    `how the applicant meets Article 11(4)(c) and (d)` IS AN `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)`
    `matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)` IS AN `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)`
    `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)` IS AN `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)`

-- src:305 | (b) a copy of the applicant’s constitution;
-- src:306 | (c) a draft of the proposed statement of the entity’s registered charitable purposes;
-- src:307 | (d) a draft of the entity’s registered public benefit statement;
@ref Article 11(2)(b) to (d) (src:305-307)
DECLARE `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` HAS
    `copy of the applicant's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `draft of the registered public benefit statement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:308 | (e) details of –
-- src:309 | (i) the applicant’s most recent, if any, financial accounts,
-- src:310 | (ii) any payment made to any governor of the entity in the 12 months preceding the application, and if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity, a draft of the proposed statement under that Order,
-- src:311 | (iii) any other financial information that would be required if the application were for registration under the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008, and
-- src:312 | (iv) if the applicant is not requesting entry in the restricted section of the register, any further financial information prescribed by the Minister by Order; and
@ref Article 11(2)(e) (src:308-312)
DECLARE `Financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` HAS
    `most recent financial accounts exist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `details of the most recent financial accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payments made to governors` IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor`
    `payments to governors disclosed in the application` IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor`
    `draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 would require other financial information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other financial information required under that Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry in the restricted section is requested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Order prescribes further financial information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `further financial information prescribed by Order` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:313 | (f) such other information, documents and evidence as may be –
-- src:314 | (i) required by Regulations under paragraph (3), or
-- src:315 | (ii) otherwise requested by the Commissioner in order to determine the application.
@ref Article 11(2)(f) (src:313-315)
DECLARE `Other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` HAS
    `Regulations under Article 11(3) require other information, documents or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `procedure under Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) followed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Commissioner has requested other information, documents or evidence to determine the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:300 | (2) The applicant must provide to the Commissioner, in such form as the Commissioner may publish in relation to an entity of a description into which that charity falls –
@ref Article 11(2) (src:300)
DECLARE `Application for registration` HAS
    dates IS A `Dates of an application`
    `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS A `Particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`
    `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS A `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)`
    `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS A `Financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`
    `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS A `Other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`
    `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS A LIST OF `Item of Article 11(2)`

-- A period of calendar days, both ends inclusive.
@ref Article 11(2)(e)(ii) (a period of calendar days, both ends inclusive)
DECLARE `Period of days` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

§§ `Article 11(4) -- the six matters and the duty of the Commissioner`

-- What Article 11(4) asks the Commissioner to be satisfied of, as far as no other group decides it. The standard inputs of the other groups (IP8, IP17, IP18, IP22 to IP24) are separate parameters.
-- Each field is the Commissioner's finding on that matter and is named for what it decides; "satisfied" is not a further input (FRAGMENT-G4.md, "modelling decisions").
-- src:319 | (4) If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that –
-- src:320 | (a) the applicant meets the charity test, or will do so on registration;
-- src:321 | (b) the constitution of the applicant is a written document;
-- src:322 | (c) the applicant –
-- src:323 | (i) is a Jersey entity, or
-- src:324 | (ii) carries out, or intends to carry out, in or from within Jersey, an activity that is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial;
-- src:325 | (d) the applicant has a principal address in Jersey, within the meaning of Article 8(4);
-- src:326 | (e) the name of the applicant is not undesirable under Article 12; and
-- src:327 | (f) no other ground for refusal, prescribed under paragraph (7), applies or should be applied.
@ref Article 11(4) (src:319-327)
DECLARE `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` HAS
    `applicant will meet the charity test on registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `constitution of the applicant is a written document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
    `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What the Commissioner must, or must not, do with an application, once the six matters, the compliance of the applicant and the bars of Articles 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c) are known.
-- The Law names two outcomes ("register", "refuse"); the other three are the cases the Law leaves between them (T10): an application that does not comply, a bar that is temporary, a bar that is not.
@ref Articles 11(4), 11(5), 19(9)(c) and 20(1)(c)
DECLARE `Duty of the Commissioner on an application for registration` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
    `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
    `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
    `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
    `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`

§§ `Article 12 -- the nouns of the name`

-- How a registered charity changes its name: by changing the registered name, or by adding an alternative registered name (Article 12(3)).
-- src:362 | (3) A registered charity may apply to the Commissioner for permission to change its registered name or to add an alternative registered name.
@ref Article 12(3) (src:362)
DECLARE `Kind of change of a registered name` IS ONE OF
    `a change of the registered name`
    `the addition of an alternative registered name`

@ref Article 12 (the acts of the Article, by role)
DECLARE `Thing done under Article 12` IS ONE OF
    `enter the name of the entity in the register as the registered name` HAS name IS A STRING
    `allocate a registration number and enter it in the register` HAS number IS A STRING
    `apply for permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name` HAS change IS A `Kind of change of a registered name`
    `refuse permission to change the registered name or to add an alternative registered name`
    `enter the new or alternative registered name in the register` HAS name IS A STRING, change IS A `Kind of change of a registered name`
    `require the charity to apply to change its registered name`
    `use a name` HAS name IS A STRING

@ref Article 12 (an act and the role that does it)
DECLARE `Act under Article 12` HAS
    actor IS A `Legal actor`
    `what is done` IS A `Thing done under Article 12`

-- Article 12(1)(a): the name "of any other registered charity" is a name in the register. A name entered in the register is described by the fact the Law turns on: whose it is (and in what standing),
-- and in what capacity it is entered. Forks F4.5, F4.7 and F4.8 read these fields.
@ref Articles 8(3)(l), 12(2), 12(3), 12(5) and 12(7)(a)
DECLARE `Kind of entry of a name in the register` IS ONE OF
    `the registered name`
    `an alternative registered name`
    `a previous registered name`

@ref Article 12(1)(a)
DECLARE `Name entered in the register` HAS
    name IS A STRING
    `kind of entry` IS A `Kind of entry of a name in the register`
    `standing of the entity that holds it` IS A `Standing on the register`
    `held by the entity itself` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Article 12(1): the four grounds on which a name is undesirable, each "in the opinion of the Commissioner". Ground (a) is the Commissioner's opinion applied to the names in the register:
-- the entries he or she is of the opinion are the same as, or too similar to, the name in question. Grounds (b) to (d) are opinions.
-- src:354 | (1) For the purpose of Article 11(4)(e), the name of an entity is undesirable as the registered name of a charity if, in the opinion of the Commissioner, the name –
-- src:355 | (a) is the same as, or too similar to, the name of any other registered charity;
-- src:356 | (b) is likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity;
-- src:357 | (c) gives the impression that the entity is connected to any person to which it is not connected, whether in Jersey or elsewhere; or
-- src:358 | (d) is offensive.
@ref Article 12(1) (src:354-358)
DECLARE `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` HAS
    `name in question` IS A STRING
    `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name` IS A LIST OF `Name entered in the register`
    `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offensive` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Article 12(7): a name that a registered charity uses, with the facts the Law turns on.
-- src:366 | (7) A registered charity must not use any name other than –
-- src:367 | (a) its registered name or one of its registered names; or
-- src:368 | (b) another name that –
-- src:369 | (i) is related to such a name, and
-- src:370 | (ii) is not, in the opinion of the Commissioner, undesirable within the meaning of paragraph (1), in the context in which it is used.
@ref Article 12(7) (src:366-370)
DECLARE `Name used by a registered charity` HAS
    `name used` IS A STRING
    `previous registered names of the charity` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `related to one of the charity's registered names` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undesirable within Article 12(1) in the context in which it is used, in the opinion of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
